# Documentation Templates

Templates and patterns for automated documentation creation, following the automated-documentation.mdc rules.

## When to Apply

Apply these templates when creating documentation following the automated-documentation.mdc rules.

## Template: Architectural Decision Record (ADR)

**Location**: `docs/decisions/DDD-description.md`  
**Format**: `DDD` = sequential number (001, 002, ...)

```markdown
---
documentation_type: decision
purpose: Document architectural decision {decision_title}
audience: developers
created_date: YYYY-MM-DD
last_updated: YYYY-MM-DD
status: active
related_docs:
  - docs/PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE.md
lifecycle: permanent
---

# Decision {DDD}: {Decision Title}

**Date**: {YYYY-MM-DD}  
**Status**: Accepted | Superseded | Deprecated  
**Supersedes**: [Decision XXX](XXX-decision.md) (if applicable)

## Context

{Why this decision was needed - 1-2 paragraphs}

- Problem statement
- Current state
- Constraints or requirements

## Decision

{What was decided - clear statement}

{Key aspects of the decision}

## Rationale

{Why this choice was made - bullet points}

- Reason 1
- Reason 2
- Reason 3

## Consequences

{What this enables/prevents - bullet points}

- Positive consequence 1
- Positive consequence 2
- Negative consequence 1 (if any)

## Alternatives Considered

### Option B: {Alternative Name}
**Why rejected**: {reason}

### Option C: {Alternative Name}
**Why rejected**: {reason}

## Related Documentation

- [Project Architecture](../PROJECT_ARCHITECTURE.md)
- [Implementation Status](../IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md)
- [Related Decision XXX](XXX-decision.md)

## Lifecycle

- **Created**: {YYYY-MM-DD}
- **Last Updated**: {YYYY-MM-DD}
- **Status**: active
- **Review By**: {YYYY-MM-DD} (if applicable)
```

